Expression Meaning <code>s = &lt;a,b,c&gt;</code> Sequence of three elements. <code>#s</code> Length of the seqeunce. <code>head s = a</code> First Element. <code>tail s = &lt;b,c&gt;</code> Remaining elements after the head. ## Example in JML Specification <pre><code>/*@ public model sequence&lt;String&gt; Messages;
    public invariant
        Messages == ("Login", "Request", "Logout");
@*/
</code></pre> ## Sequence Operations ### Sequence Length - The length of a sequence is written as <code>|sequence|</code> - It represents the number of elements in the sequence. <p>Example</p> <ul> <li><code>|[]| = 0</code> (the empty sequence has a length of 0)</li> <li>Let <code>t = [23, 44, 42, 1, 99]</code></li> <li><code>|t| = 5</code></li> <li>Let <code>Contents = [[a, b], [c, d], [e, f]]</code></li> <li><code>|Contents| = 3</code> (length counts top-level elements, not nested ones)</li> </ul>
